4. CONVEX COST MODEL
================================================================================

The core rule:
- Query = live reads.
- Mutation = durable truth, authz, intent capture, no-clobber gates, and scheduled handoff.
- Action = expensive outside work only.
- Workflow / scheduled functions = durable background orchestration.

Query
- Best for app reads.
- Reactive, cached, consistent, and cheap relative to actions.
- Cannot call external APIs.
- Still consumes function calls and database I/O.

Mutation
- Best for writes, idempotency, admission control, and invariant enforcement.
- Transactional and deterministic.
- Correct place to record user intent and schedule later work atomically.
- Still consumes function calls, write throughput, and database I/O.

Action
- Best only for external APIs, model calls, fetch, Node libraries, and long-running side effects.
- Not atomic and not reactive/cached like queries.
- Action compute is the costlier lane; Node actions are more expensive than Convex-runtime functions.
- Actions that call many ctx.runQuery / ctx.runMutation calls also create more function calls, DB I/O, and separate transactions.

NodeRoom pattern
- Do not run an action for every keystroke.
- Save edits through mutations.
- Enqueue/debounce passive activity server-side.
- Use queries for live UI/status.
- Use workflows/actions only after the saved content is noteworthy and cache/local evidence is insufficient.

