How the passive “noteworthy” pipeline now fits

Current repo reality: the latest code already reflects this direction. Public room-agent messages are primarily @nodeagent in src/ui/Chat.tsx, route/model choice comes from the composer picker, src/app/store.tsx mainly calls api.agentJobs.start, and convex/agentJobs.ts centralizes durable starts through startDurableAgentJob(...).

The new pipeline is:

User types into notebook / spreadsheet / wiki
  -> client saves durable node/cell/wiki/message
  -> client calls debounceActivityScan once per saved object
  -> Convex cancels previous scheduled scan for same source
  -> quiet window passes
  -> scanActivity re-reads latest committed content
  -> cheap classifier decides whether it is noteworthy
  -> creates passive agentJob + entityWorkItems
  -> later workflow handles research / cache / evidence / OKF

In plain language:

We let the user type freely. We do not bother the agent until the user pauses. We do not call external APIs inside the scanner. We only create durable work items if the saved content looks like a person, company, product, topic, task, source, or research lead.

This is the right extension of the MewAgent history: user writes notes, the system creates backlinks, claims, tasks, and research work around those notes, but the user’s original note remains theirs.

The uploaded file also matches this architecture: it distinguishes a clean NodeAgent harness from raw model behavior, argues that evidence capture should feed BankerToolBench-style tasks, and recommends Firecrawl first, Stagehand/Browserbase only when exact box fidelity is required.

