5. Payment handling: my recommendation

NodeRoom needs two ledgers:

1. Billing ledger
   provider customers, subscriptions, invoices, checkout sessions, webhooks

2. Usage ledger
   model tokens, search calls, source captures, file GB, transcode minutes,
   workflow runtime, agent jobs, OKF exports

Do not let the agent mutate entitlements directly.

Payment provider webhooks update entitlements. Agents can explain billing or draft a support note, but the backend billing webhook is the source of truth.

Provider choice
Provider	Best for NodeRoom	Tradeoff
Stripe	Enterprise/B2B control, invoices, procurement, custom pricing, serious SaaS billing. Convex has a Stripe starter showing checkout + webhook fulfillment.	You own tax/compliance complexity unless using Stripe Tax and proper setup.
Polar	Usage-based billing and developer-friendly metering. Polar docs support event-ingested usage meters and metered billing, including token/file/video-style meters.	Younger ecosystem; verify fit for enterprise procurement.
Dodo Payments	Merchant-of-record route with Convex component, checkout, customer portal, webhooks, subscriptions, and on-demand charges.	Less standard than Stripe for large enterprise finance teams.
Lemon Squeezy	Simple MoR for SaaS/digital goods; handles payments, taxes/VAT/compliance/fraud, and supports many currencies.	May be less flexible for complex enterprise usage-based billing.
Practical recommendation

For tomorrow / early product:

Use Stripe-style internal schema design,
but consider Polar or Dodo for early usage-based/MoR if tax/admin burden matters.

For enterprise finance customers:

Stripe first.

For solo/SMB launch speed:

Polar or Dodo if MoR/usage-based simplicity is more important than enterprise procurement.
